      summary:'Offer a genuine opportunity to change his conduct. Present a bounded argument, ask for an observable action and retain protection if he refuses. Understanding his grief does not settle accountability.',
      prerequisites:[
        p('persuade-meeting','Establish a real opportunity for dialogue','Choose an actually reached place or agreed channel, who can leave, what interrupts the meeting and which controls remain watched. A projection can receive an argument but does not demonstrate that a remote apparatus was stopped.',['glass-restoration'],'access'),
        p('persuade-case','Prepare a corroborated argument','Identify the party’s specific claim, its independent supporting observations and its strongest uncertainty. Personal family history may help but no private character confession is required.',['glass-contradictions','family-brief-reunion','family-identity-open'],'evidence'),
        p('persuade-terms','Ask for a verifiable first action','Request a concrete pause, isolation of a named connection, access for an independent observer or surrender of a particular control. Agree how the action will be verified before exchanging testimony or components.',['district-expansion','district-interventions'],'plan'),
        p('persuade-voices','Let affected people choose representation','Invite willing residents or a survivor to speak directly, submit a limited statement, use a chosen representative or decline. They do not owe Halaster a confrontation, forgiveness or a performance of suffering.',['district-coupling'],'consent'),
        p('persuade-fallback','Maintain an independent fallback','Keep actual warning, exit and intervention plans ready. Record which concessions can be reversed and how noncompliance will be detected; no promise disables the party’s alternatives automatically.',['district-interventions'],'plan')
      ],
