  const encounterBranches = [
    {id:'branch-before',title:'Before activation: an interruption or heist',detail:'The current plan has a real missing prerequisite. The party can negotiate access, secure a delivery, copy records or interrupt an accessible segment. Use published inhabitants and current allies at the actual location.',objectives:['Reach the specific prerequisite without assuming a safe route.','Confirm what the intervention changes.','Leave with an honest report or a maintained interruption.'],changes:['A failed stealth attempt changes the response of a witness who actually noticed it.','A successful interruption delays the associated work; another method requires a concrete preparation and visible trace.'],fallback:'Protect the threatened area and investigate the next actual preparation. Failure does not cause instantaneous activation.'},
    {id:'branch-dialogue',title:'Dialogue while others prepare',detail:'Let a willing speaker meet Halaster while separate willing helpers carry out agreed city preparations. Use actual communication and elapsed travel; no automatic real-time contact between city and floor 23.',objectives:['Seek an observable concession.','Preserve exit and independent checks.','Keep resident choices and limited disclosures intact.'],changes:['A verified concession pauses the relevant process.','A broken agreement informs trust and the next response without dictating permanent hostility or forgiveness.'],fallback:'Withdraw from the meeting or change approaches; preserve successful warning and evacuation work.'},
    {id:'branch-combat',title:'Combat around separate objectives',detail:'If fighting occurs, use Halaster’s supplied published stat block and the actual room’s inhabitants, geometry and hazards. Put the inspected apparatus objectives in view with separate progress and state. Do not equate his HP with the machine’s condition.',objectives:['Protect reachable people and routes.','Perform only established apparatus interactions.','Respond to Halaster’s actual actions, including escape, surrender or defeat.'],changes:['At each clear event, report which objective changed and the source of that change.','A failed control interaction can cost position or time as announced; essential acquired knowledge remains available.'],fallback:'Retreat, negotiate a pause, isolate a different verified branch or continue city protection. Use actual capabilities and ordinary rules; this card supplies no new spell immunity, automatic counterspell or invented boss phase.'},
    {id:'branch-active',title:'Activation: several partial successes',detail:'When activation actually begins, run an agreed sequence of observed changes. Alternate the party’s chosen location with brief reports from helpers whose communication is established. Each group’s known success remains effective unless a concrete new event changes it.',objectives:['Confirm the warning reached named recipients.','Keep one verified route or refuge viable.','Reach a tested control or document why it is inaccessible.'],changes:['Only advance a danger step when the current apparatus action and elapsed play support it.','A new obstruction affects its actual route; an unaffected route stays usable.'],fallback:'Prioritize people, withdraw beyond tested limits and preserve accurate information for a later attempt. Do not predetermine loss of the district.'},
    {id:'branch-halaster-down',title:'Halaster is defeated, absent or withdrawn',detail:'Record his actual condition separately, then check the apparatus. Defeat may create access or time without changing active controls. If he died in Undermountain, use the published 1d10-day rejuvenation and later preparations based on actual events.',objectives:['Determine what remains running.','Protect people and secure reachable hazards.','Plan monitoring and access for the interval and possible return.'],changes:['A surrendered key or performed shutdown matters because it occurred, not because he lost HP.','A future rejuvenation is a rule-based pending development; do not announce its exact result to players without an earned source.'],fallback:'Apparatus work continues with whatever controls, allies and records are actually available.'},
    {id:'branch-limited',title:'A limited attempt produces an unexpected person or answer',detail:'If the reviewed method actually yields contact or presence, give the individual a voice and ordinary choices. Identity, stability and desire are separate observations. No outcome is preselected by this card.',objectives:['Ask what they want and whether communication may continue.','Observe the agreed safety limit and care plan.','Keep testimony private to its chosen audience.'],changes:['A refusal ends the attempted contact according to the established humane stop plan.','An unexpected identity or wish becomes evidence to review, not an excuse to enlarge the trial.'],fallback:'Stop, maintain agreed care, preserve an accurate limited record or continue research later.'}
  ];

